WOW-BG3 benilla patch 0037: the figures' materials as BG3 shades them, under WoW's light (on top of
0001-0009, 0011-0036).

The characters must look as they do in BG3, only with WoW's lighting; their detail and porous skin
visible. Before, patch 0006's law drew them as WoW's diffuse (`albedo x lit`) with a restrained GGX of the sun:
metal kept its whole albedo as diffuse (Lae'zel's armour white), hair showed its reddish-brown G-buffer base colour
without BG3's strand lighting (Tav's blonde hair), the skin had no sheen and none of BG3's tiled detail normals
(its pores), and the normal and surface maps were raw texture layers, not what BG3's shaders make of them. Here:
- wow_model.wgsl (`WOW_TAV_SURFACE`, `tav_fetch`, `tav_bg3`): BG3's lighting of its G-buffer values
  (`Shaders/Vulkan/ClusteredLighting/*.bshd` in EngineShaders.pak): Frostbite's GGX with the sun as a disc, the
  height-correlated Smith visibility and BG3's specular antialiasing; diffuse colour albedo x (1 - metalness), F0
  0.16 x specular^2 toward the albedo by metalness, the split-sum environment; the skin's dual specular lobes from
  its diffusion profile, its thin-object transmission and (a stand-in for BG3's screen-space diffusion) the normal
  flattened per colour by the profile; UE4's hair (R, TT, TRT, its diffuse) along BG3's strand direction. The
  light is WoW's: its lit term per normal as the irradiance multiplier (a plain diffuse surface keeps patch 0006's
  `albedo x lit` exactly), the sun's radiance pi x (lit(L) - ambient), WoW's ambient as the environment, point
  lights, entity shade, fog and the mouseover highlight as WoW adds them. Units as patch 0006 (measured in world
  mode: the albedo samples linear and the pass's output reaches the frame sRGB-encoded): linear radiance out;
  flag 16 (WOW_BG3_TAV_OUT=gamma) writes it sRGB-encoded instead. Detail normal maps tiled at BG3's tiling.
  tav_a.x < 0 keeps patch 0006's law; tav_a.z the debug view (1 to 10, without the highlight; 8 is 0006's law).
- materials.rs: WowModelExt lanes tav_a..tav_d (zero on every WoW material; model_render.rs and
  world_assets/mod.rs set them so).
- wowbg3_tav.rs: tavtex.txt's 0037 tokens (model:, extra:, detail:, profile:), the extra map in the emissive slot
  and the detail normal map in the occlusion slot, albedo mip chains of tavtex (TVT flag 8), the debug view
  (`tavdebug`), WOW_BG3_TAV_SHADE=wow (patch 0006's law, rollback), WOW_BG3_TAV_OUT=gamma.

